{"seq":21,"ts_us":1793632780061526,"service":"agentd","trace_id":"adb1650a118f89e4f327d673df7880cf","payload":{"kind":"ag_ui","type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"call_7655cda5a1ac4a4788393de5","delta":"{\"text\":\"Here's what I found (read-only \\u2014 I changed nothing).\\n\\nComponent states: all four are reported \\\"unknown\\\" because their sysfs nodes aren't readable \\u2014 screen (sys/class/backlight/lcd/brightness, card0-DSI-1/bl_power), bluetooth (sys/class/bluetooth/hci0/state), wifi (sys/class/net/wlan0/operstate). local_model is unknown too, and there's no local_url configured, so there's no local model to watch. Only \\\"services\\\" is definitively off: 0 running services in the svcd executor. Idle is 4s against a 2s timeout, but a request is in flight (this one).\\n\\nThe idle plan is a dry run \\u2014 it names commands, agentd never runs them:\\n- Bluetooth: propose off \\u2014 `rfkill block bluetooth` (idle, nothing needs it).\\n- Services: propose off \\u2014 no command needed, already off.\\n- Screen, wifi, local_model: keep, because a request is in flight.\\n\\nNote agentd can't switch any of these itself; only local_model is flagged as agentd-switchable, and an operator would run the radio/screen/Bluetooth commands.\"}"}}
